  "metadata": {
    "job": "Plate with four mounting feet",
    "revision": "A",
    "notes": "The four feet are INSTANCES of one block definition, not copies — edit the definition and all four follow. Rigid means the solver gives the degrees of freedom to the block as a whole — three per instance, x/y/angle, however many circles it holds. Hold one with `fixed`: a fixedPoint on a member lives INSIDE the block, and internal constraints are dropped, so it does nothing at all. Each instance is rotated a quarter turn more, so every anti-rotation dowel points in toward the plate centre."
  },
